# Round 70: `report of <never-bound-name>` answered "equilibrium" rc 0
# where the VM raises "undefined variable" rc 1 -- aot_report conflated
# two distinct env misses (never-bound vs bound-but-unobserved) into the
# "equilibrium" arm, while its sibling aot_predicate_of ten lines up had
# the split all along (which is why `stable of zzz` died correctly). The
# name skips every static guard by construction: the top-level order
# guard only covers names IN g_module_names, and zzz is bound nowhere.
# aot_report now mirrors the sibling: never-bound raises; a compiled
# function (env-unbound here, bound in the VM) reports "equilibrium" via
# the unobserved-slot band; bound-but-unobserved stays "equilibrium".
# _err class: both die "undefined variable 'zzz'", equal codes.
x is 1.0
x is 2.0
print of (str of (stable of x))
print of (report of zzz)
